WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.700
A seed can become a huge tree while the soil hardly shrinks.

2
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.060
What becomes the wood?

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.000
Watch one tiny seed beside a growing trunk.

4
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.960
The tree gains layer after layer.

5
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.700
The soil gauge barely moves.

6
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.440
Something outside the soil must supply most of that new material.

7
00:00:23.967 --> 00:00:26.147
Start by sorting matter from energy.

8
00:00:27.647 --> 00:00:30.107
Matter has mass and can become part of the tree.

9
00:00:31.527 --> 00:00:34.847
Energy can move or change form, but it does not become wood.

10
00:00:36.287 --> 00:00:38.727
Sunlight reaches the leaf as radiant energy.

11
00:00:39.947 --> 00:00:45.107
It powers the building, the way electricity runs a factory's machines without

12
00:00:45.107 --> 00:00:46.427
becoming part of the product.

13
00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.130
Water enters through roots and moves upward.

14
00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.910
Carbon dioxide enters leaves from the air.

15
00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.770
Light arrives at those leaves too.

16
00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:02.930
The plant uses the light energy to build sugar from carbon dioxide and water.

17
00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.150
Oxygen leaves as another product.

18
00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:10.430
The word equation is a summary, not one single step.

19
00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:11.310
The word equation is a summary, not one single step.

20
00:01:11.483 --> 00:01:16.203
Now predict. Which paths carry matter that can enter the trunk?

21
00:01:17.463 --> 00:01:19.103
Which path carries only energy?

22
00:01:20.483 --> 00:01:22.743
Follow each colour before the tree grows again.

23
00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:32.597
The teal carbon dioxide and blue water paths carry matter.

24
00:01:33.797 --> 00:01:35.617
The gold light path carries energy.

25
00:01:36.997 --> 00:01:41.657
Light powers sugar-building from carbon dioxide and water; conditions limit its

26
00:01:41.657 --> 00:01:45.697
speed. The first half explains what can become wood.

27
00:01:46.997 --> 00:01:50.957
The second half reminds us that building cannot always run faster.

28
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.940
In plants and algae, this work happens inside chloroplasts.

29
00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.600
Chloroplasts are green parts of some cells, mostly in leaves.

30
00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.840
Chlorophyll inside them captures radiant energy.

31
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.660
Roots, which sit in darkness, usually have no chloroplasts.

32
00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:14.360
Photosynthetic bacteria do the work without chloroplasts.

33
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:17.573
Sugar does not have one destination.

34
00:02:19.173 --> 00:02:22.033
Some is used now as cells release energy for living.

35
00:02:23.333 --> 00:02:25.073
Some is linked into starch and stored.

36
00:02:26.413 --> 00:02:28.553
Some is rebuilt into wood and new leaves.

37
00:02:29.913 --> 00:02:33.253
Each route starts with the same green sugar block made in the leaf.

38
00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:37.803
That stored chemical energy can move through a food web.

39
00:02:39.043 --> 00:02:41.863
A rabbit eats clover, and a fox eats the rabbit.

40
00:02:43.123 --> 00:02:45.723
Both depend on energy captured by a producer.

41
00:02:47.283 --> 00:02:49.623
Almost every food web begins this way.

42
00:02:50.823 --> 00:02:53.963
A few communities use chemical energy instead of light.

43
00:02:55.017 --> 00:02:56.337
Return to the tree.

44
00:02:57.717 --> 00:02:59.777
Its soil did not need to become the trunk.

45
00:03:01.377 --> 00:03:05.977
Matter arrived mainly as carbon dioxide, with water also supplying atoms.

46
00:03:07.597 --> 00:03:09.537
Light supplied the energy for building sugar.

47
00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:15.237
Light supplies the energy; carbon dioxide and water supply the matter.

48
00:03:16.417 --> 00:03:20.717
The plant then used that sugar to make living material and feed other life.
